0..73 Comment "// The syntax\'s constructors and operations respect paths: the successor,"
74..151 Comment "// a variable, an abstraction, weakening and a substitution each carry a path"
152..226 Comment "// between their arguments to one between their results. `Path.ap` takes a"
227..296 Comment "// named function, so each constructor is given one; a substitution\'s"
297..355 Comment "// congruence in its term is a `Path.walk` along the path."
357..406 Comment "// The naturals; the syntax and its substitution."
